      "HELEN: I made a kelp salad. - -\nENOLA: We always have kelp salad.\nHELEN: It's good for you.\nENOLA: I'm not hungry.",
      "HELEN: Take the bird too. I don't want them to find it. Helen grabs an oxygen cannister and checks the valve. She puts it in the barrel with Enola.\nHELEN: It's set so you have air for an hour. Don't touch the valve. If you overpressurize, they might see the bubbles.\nENOLA: You said we we're going to win. So why do I have to hide? A little tear begins to snake its way down Enola’s cheek.\nHELEN: Go on, dolphin. Be brave. She reaches inside a pouch and pulls out two circular glass pendants. Clear crystal medallions, protected in leath…",
      "HELEN: Hold it right there!\nENOLA: What is it?\nHELEN: I don't know. Quick...",
      "ENOLA: I'm not hungry.\nHELEN: Enola, come back here and finish your dinner! Can you get her, please?",
      "HELEN: We wouldn't stand a chance out there.\nENOLA: You can't do that to us! She's still hurt."
    ]
